  Yo!

  I needed to decode the hexadecimal substring, so I wrote [Hexen], yet
  another library for encoding and decoding hexadecimal byte sequences.

  The main goal of this library is to provide a flexible API for
  encoding and decoding substrings into any destination (bytes or
  buffers).


[Hexen] <https://github.com/dx3mod/hexen>

Usage
=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C

  Hexen provides high-level functions like `encode' and `decode' for
  quick encoding and decoding of strings or substrings.

  =E2=94=8C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.encode "Hello World";;
  =E2=94=82 (* - : string =3D "48656c6c6f20576f726c64" *)
  =E2=94=82=20
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.decode "48656c6c6f20576f726c64";;
  =E2=94=82 (* - : string =3D "Hello World" *)
  =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80

  =E2=94=8C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.encode_substring "Hello World" 0 5;;
  =E2=94=82 (* - : string =3D "48656c6c6f" *)
  =E2=94=82=20
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.decode_substring "48656c6c6f20576f726c64" 0 10;;
  =E2=94=82 (* - : string =3D "Hello" *)
  =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80

  Also, Hexen provides functions to encode and decode strings or
  substrings directly into existing buffers or bytes.

  =E2=94=8C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80
  =E2=94=82 let buffer =3D Buffer.create 16 in
  =E2=94=82=20
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.encode_to_buffer "Hello" buffer;
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.encode_substring_to_buffer "Hello World" 5 6 buffer;
  =E2=94=82=20
  =E2=94=82 let bytes =3D Bytes.create 12 in=20
  =E2=94=82 Hexen.decode_into (Buffer.contents buffer) 0 bytes 0 22;
  =E2=94=82 Bytes.set bytes 11 '!';
  =E2=94=82=20
  =E2=94=82 bytes
  =E2=94=82 (* - : bytes =3D Bytes.of_string "Hello World!" *)
