  *Multiple issues in Marshal*

  Several issues have been discovered in the Marshal module:

  ANT-2026-K7NTK0FT Stale obj_counter across unmarshal calls enables
  null/freed intern_obj_table indexing

  ANT-2026-2NJYQWEX Custom block size wraparound in CODE_CUSTOM_LEN
  allocation

  ANT-2026-PJC00M7X Unmarshaler accepts forged Closure_tag metadata
  without validation

  This is a followup for [OSEC-2026-01]

  Corrupted or malicious marshaled data that causes undefined behaviour
  in the runtime system when unmarshaled. input_value should either fail
  cleanly or produce a well-formed OCaml object, without corrupting the
  runtime system.

  Consequently, this excludes well-formed marshaled data that produces
  an OCaml object that is not of the type expected by the OCaml code and
  causes the Ocaml code to crash or misbehave.


[OSEC-2026-01] <https://osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-01>

