  ANT-2026-R7FKP7RG Win32 quote_cmd_filename misses pipe/redirect
  metacharacters

  ANT-2026-SRZZ62SD Windows batch-file argument injection via
  maybe_quote/make_cmdline

  ANT-2026-JPEWMPAB Win32 argument quoting leaves embedded CR/LF
  unescaped

  Also includes the fix for [OSEC-2026-05]

  `Filename.quote_command' returns a quoted command line, suitable for
  use as an argument to `Sys.command', `Unix.system', and the
  `Unix.open_process' functions.  However on Windows certain characters
  weren't properly escaped.

  `Unix.create_process' can invoke `.bat' or `.cmd' programs on Windows,
  and certain characters were accepted that cannot be quoted safely.


[OSEC-2026-05] <https://osv.dev/vulnerability/OSEC-2026-05>

Fix
=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C=E2=95=8C

  `Filename.quote_command' has been updated to correctly quote
  arguments.  `Unix.create_process*' has been updated to reject
  arguments that cannot be safely quoted by raising `Failure':
        if the program [prog] is a [.bat] or [.cmd] script and
        either [prog] or [args] contain characters that cannot be
        securely passed to a script, such as [" | & , ; < =3D > ^ %
        "].  If you really need to pass these characters to a
        script, consider using {!Unix.system} instead.


